{\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;\H0.5x;1. WORK SHALL CONFORM TO ALL APPLICABLE CODES AND ORDINANCES, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO: BUILDING, PLUMBING, ELECTRICAL, AND MECHANICAL CODES. \P\fLucida Grande|b0|i0|c0|p34; \P\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;2. ANY ERRORS, OMISS
  3
IONS, OR CONFLICTS FOUND WITHIN THESE DRAWINGS SHALL BE BROUGHT TO THE ATTENTION OF THE OWNER OR THEIR REPRESENTATIVE BEFORE PROCEEDING WITH THE WORK.\P\fLucida Grande|b0|i0|c0|p34; \P\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;3. DO NOT SCALE THESE DRAWINGS. WRITTEN DIMEN
  3
SIONS TAKE PRECEDENCE OVER MEASUREMENTS.\P\fLucida Grande|b0|i0|c0|p34; \P\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;4. DIMENSIONS ARE TAKEN FROM FACE OF FRAMING LUMBER, FACE OF CONCRETE/ MASONRY, CENTER OF COLUMN, AND CENTERLINE OF FIXTURE, UNLESS NOTED OTHERWISE.\P\fLuc
  3
ida Grande|b0|i0|c0|p34; \P\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;5. ALL DIMENSIONS NOTED "VERIFY IN FIELD (V.I.F.)" SHALL BE MEASURED BY THE CONTRACTOR PRIOR TO CONSTRUCTION. REPORT ANY DISCREPANCIES TO THE OWNER OR THEIR REPRESENTATIVE.\P\fLucida Grande|b0|i0|c0|p34
  3
; \P\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;6. DETAILS SHOWN ARE TYPICAL. SIMILAR DETAILS APPLY IN SIMILAR SITUATIONS.\P\fLucida Grande|b0|i0|c0|p34; \P\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;7. IN THE CASE OF DISCREPANCIES WITHIN DESCRIPTIONS OF SIMILAR ITEMS, PRECEDENCE SHALL BE GIVEN 
  3
TO NOTES & DRAWINGS OF GREATER DETAIL.\P\fLucida Grande|b0|i0|c0|p34; \P\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;8. ALL REQUIRED EXITS SHALL BE OPERABLE FROM THE INSIDE, WITHOUT THE USE OF A KEY OR ANY SPECIAL KNOWLEDGE. \P\fLucida Grande|b0|i0|c0|p34; \P\fArial|b0|i0|c
  3
0|p34;9. ANY ELECTRICAL, PLUMBING AND/OR HVAC SYSTEMS INCLUDED IN THE WORK SHALL BE INSTALLED ON A DESIGN-BUILD BASIS, AND SHALL NOT SIGNIFICANTLY ALTER THE STRUCTURE OR FINISHES.\P\P10. SMOKE DETECTORS AND CARBON MONOXIDE DETECTORS SHALL BE INSTALLE
  3
D PER APPLICABLE CODES.\P\P11. GRADING AND SITEWORK SHALL BE MINIMAL IN ALL AREAS NOT DIRECTLY AFFECTED BY CONSTRUCTION. FOLLOW BEST PRACTICES AND LOCAL REQUIREMENTS IN ORDER TO MINIMIZE ENVIRONMENTAL DAMAGE.\P\P12. FINISH GRADE MUST SLOPE AWAY FROM 
  3
EXTERIOR FOUNDATION WALL, AT A HEIGHT OF 6 INCHES OVER A 10 FOOT DISTANCE.\P\P13. ANY SURVEY MARKERS WITHIN THE AREA OF CONSTRUCTION SHALL BE PRESERVED OR RESET BY A REGISTERED CIVIL ENGINEER OR LICENSED LAND SURVEYOR.\P\P14. BEFORE GRADING OPERATION
  3
S, A TEMPORARY PROTECTION FENCE SHALL BE CONSTRUCTED AROUND ANY TREE WITHIN 30 FEET OF THE FOUNDATION, AND A SILT FENCE MUST BE CONSTRUCTED DOWNSLOPE OF ANY AREA WHERE THE SOIL IS DISTURBED.\P\P\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p0;15. DEPICTED FOUNDATION SHOWS ONLY A
  3
 PROPOSED DESIGN BASED ON FICTIONAL CONDITIONS. CONDUCT A SOIL TEST AND STRUCTURAL ENGINEERING FOR A SITE-SPECIFIC FOUNDATION.^J^J16. FOOTINGS SHALL EXTEND DOWN BEYOND THE LOCAL FROST LINE. ^J^J17. PERFORATED DRAIN PIPES SHALL BE LOCATED WITHIN A GRAVEL 
  3
PERIMETER AROUND THE FOUNDATION, WITH MULTIPLE DRAINAGE OUTLETS LEADING DOWNSLOPE AWAY FROM THE BUILDING.^J^J18. FIRE BLOCKING AND FIRE-RATED SHEATHING SHALL BE PROVIDED AS REQUIRED AT CEILINGS, FLOORS, AND ENCLOSED USABLE SPACE UNDER STAIRS.\fLucida G
  3
rande|b0|i0|c0|p34;^J^J\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p0;19. ALL WOOD WITHIN 8 INCHES OF THE GROUND SHALL BE PRESSURE TREATED OR COMPRISE A SUITABLY ROT RESISTANT MATERIAL. METAL CONNECTIONS WHICH TOUCH THIS WOOD SHOULD BE GALVANIZED OR STAINLESS STEEL.^J^J20 PROVIDE 
  3
ADEQUATE BLOCKING AROUND CABINETRY, PLUMBING FIXTURES, AND OTHER APPLICABLE AREAS.^J^J21. PROVIDE MINIMUM R-13 INSULATION IN ALL EXTERIOR WALLS & R-21 INSULATION ABOVE CONDITIONED SPACES.^J^J22. DEPICTED WEATHERPROOFING METHODS (SUCH AS SEALANT, CAULKING
  1
, AND FLASHING) ARE NOT COMPREHENSIVE. FOLLOW REQUIREMENTS AND RECOMMENDATIONS OF BUILDING CODES, PRODUCT MANUFACTURERS, AND INDUSTRY BEST PRACTICES.}
