\A1;{\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;\H0.5x;23. CONTRACTOR TO ENSURE THAT INTERIOR SHEATHING IS FLUSH, CLEAN AND FREE OF DUST AND DEFECTS BEFORE APPLICATION OF PAINT COATINGS.\P\P24. FLOOR MATERIAL TRANSITIONS OCCUR AT THE CENTERLINE OF DOORS OR FRAMED OPENINGS
  3
.\P\P25. PROVIDE ONE COAT PRIMER AND TWO FINISH COATS OF PAINT AT INTERIOR AND EXTERIOR SURFACES.\P\fLucida Grande|b0|i0|c0|p34; \P\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;26. ALL GLASS SHALL CONFORM WITH HUMAN IMPACT AND SAFETY  REQUIREMENTS.\P\P27. THE MINIMUM STAIRCA
  3
SE TREAD SHALL BE 10" AND THE MAXIMUM RISER 7.75", WITH A MAXIMUM \H0.7x;\S3#8;\H1.42857x;" VARIATION WITHIN A FLIGHT.\P\P28. HANDRAILS SHALL BE LOCATED 34-38 INCHES ABOVE STAIR TREADS, AS MEASURED FROM THE NOSINGS.\P\P29. GUARDRAILS SHALL BE LOCATED
  3
 ALONG ANY FLOOR EDGES THAT DROP 30 INCHES OR MORE TO THE FLOOR OR GROUND BELOW.\P\P30. DO NOT USE SCREW-ON, NON-OPERABLE WINDOW SHUTTERS. THEY ARE AS TACKY AS CLIP-ON TIES. DO NOT USE VINYL OR ALUMINUM SIDING. THAT WOULD MAKE THIS HOUSE LOOK LIKE A 
  3
CHEAP PLASTIC TOY.\P\P\A0;31. ALL CONSTRUCTION SHALL BE TRUE, PLUMB, LEVEL, SQUARE, AND IN PROPER ALIGNMENT.\P\P32. THE GENERAL CONTRACTOR SHALL MAINTAIN A CURRENT AND COMPLETE SET OF DRAWINGS ON THE JOB SITE DURING ALL PHASES OF CONSTRUCTION. ALL SU
  3
BCONTRACTORS SHALL BE PROVIDED WITH A SET OF DRAWINGS.\P\fLucida Grande|b0|i0|c0|p34; \P\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;33. THE GENERAL CONTRACTOR SHALL VERIFY AND ASSUME RESPONSIBILITY FOR ALL DIMENSIONS AND SITE CONDITIONS, AS WELL AS INSPECT THE PREMISES AND
  3
 TAKE NOTE OF EXISTING CONDITIONS PRIOR TO SUBMITTING PRICES. NO CLAIM SHALL BE ALLOWED FOR PROBLEMS WHICH COULD HAVE BEEN PREVENTED BY A THOROUGH EXAMINATION.\P\P\H1.00002x;34. PROVIDE TEMPORARY SUPPORT AS NECESSARY TO ENSURE THE STRUCTURAL INTEGRIT
  3
Y OF THE BUILDING UNDER CONSTRUCTION. THE GENERAL CONTRACTOR IS RESPONSIBLE FOR ALL CONSTRUCTION-RELATED ACTIVITIES.\P\P\H0.99999x;35. INSTALL FIXTURES, MATERIALS, AND EQUIPMENT ACCORDING TO MANUFACTURER'S SPECIFICATIONS. SHOULD THOSE SPECS CONFLICT 
  3
WITH THE DRAWINGS, IMMEDIATELY NOTIFY THE OWNER OR THE OWNER'S REPRESENTATIVE.\P\fLucida Grande|b0|i0|c0|p34;\P\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;\H1.00001x;36. VERIFY CLEARANCES FOR FIXTURES, VENTS, CHASES, ETC. BEFORE ORDERING OR INSTALLING RELATED WORK ITEMS.\P
  3
\fLucida Grande|b0|i0|c0|p34;\P\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;\H0.99999x;37. COORDINATE ALL WORK WITH EXISTING CONDITIONS, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO: IRRIGATION PIPES, ELECTRICAL CONDUITS, WATER LINES, GAS LINES, AND DRAINAGE LINES.\P\fLucida Grande|b0|i0|c
  3
0|p34;\H1.00001x; \P\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;38. THE GENERAL CONTRACTOR SHALL BE RESPONSIBLE FOR REGULARLY REMOVING THE WASTE MATERIALS OF ALL SUBCONTRACTORS, AND MAINTAIN STRICT CONTROL OVER JOB CLEANING TO PREVENT DUST AND RUBBISH FROM INTERFERING WITH
  3
 OPERATIONS.\P\fLucida Grande|b0|i0|c0|p34; \P\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;39. CONSTRUCTION EQUIPMENT NOISE SHALL BE MINIMIZED DURING THE CONSTRUCTION PHASES BY MUFFLING AND SHIELDING IMPACT TOOLS WHENEVER POSSIBLE.\P\P40. IF THE WORK OF ANY CONTRACTOR DEVIA
  1
TES FROM THE CONTRACT DRAWINGS WITHOUT THEM FIRST GETTING PERMISSION FROM THE APPROPRIATE PROFESSIONAL, THAT CONTRACTOR MAY BE REQUIRED TO FIX THEIR WORK AT THEIR OWN EXPENSE.}
